# Platy - ownership of the boundary control mechanism
#
# RFP B.8: "Every pull request is reviewed by a senior profile before merging -
# a stronger requirement for any offshore team, where code review is the main
# remote quality safety net."
#
# A boundary rule anyone can silently relax is not a control. These paths are the
# enforcement mechanism itself, so changing them requires senior review from a
# CODEOWNER - which is the same answer to B.8, expressed as tooling rather than
# as a promise about process.
#
# Replace @tahirwaleed399 with the GitHub team handle once the client org exists.

# The boundary rules (R1-R5).
/.dependency-cruiser.cjs        @tahirwaleed399

# The CI job that blocks the merge, and repo ownership itself.
/.github/                       @tahirwaleed399

# The architecture tests, including the evasion suite.
/tests/architecture/            @tahirwaleed399

# Coverage thresholds, including the B.8 100% chain-reaction gates.
/vitest.config.ts               @tahirwaleed399

# The cross-module wire format. Changing a contract is an architecture decision:
# in Phase 2 these payloads become network payloads between services.
/src/contracts/                 @tahirwaleed399

# Module ownership boundaries in the shared database (rule R3).
/src/platform/db/schema/        @tahirwaleed399
